 ## Operating characteristics
 - **Time Complexity:** Initialization is $O(1)$ for memory mapping setup, but actual data access incurs page fault latency [G]. Total load time is proportional to the amount of data accessed, not the file size [G].
-- **Memory Complexity:** $O(1)$ relative to file size for the mapping overhead, plus the memory required for the accessed tiles. Significantly lower than eager loading for sparse or large grids [G].
-- **Measured Performance:** Effective for scenes where only a fraction of the volume is visible or processed at any time. Performance degrades if the working set exceeds physical RAM, causing thrashing [G].
-- **Strengths:** Drastically reduces peak memory usage for large VDB files. Enables loading of files larger than available RAM (provided the working set fits) [G].
-- **Limitations:** Not suitable for concurrent modification of source files without copying. Page faults can cause latency spikes during initial access [S1, unofficial].
